    "### Skewness\n",
    "\n",
    "**Skewness** measures asymmetry:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Positive skew** (right tail): mean > median, long tail to the right. Common in income, house prices, click counts.\n",
    "- **Negative skew** (left tail): mean < median, long tail to the left. Common in exam scores (most score high, few fail badly).\n",
    "- **Zero skew**: symmetric (like the normal distribution).\n",
    "\n",
    "Why does skewness matter for ML? Many algorithms assume normally distributed errors. If your target is heavily skewed, you may need a log transform. Skewed features can also distort distance-based methods (KNN, K-Means)."
   ]
  },
