    "### Failure Case: Mean Misleads with Outliers\n",
    "\n",
    "The classic failure: reporting the mean of a skewed distribution with outliers gives a misleading picture. This is why median and IQR are preferred for skewed data (e.g. salaries, house prices). Real-world consequence: if a company reports \"average salary\" as $295k but the median is $53k, most employees are being underrepresented."
   ]
  },
