   "source": [
    "### When to Use vs When NOT to Use\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use descriptive statistics:**\n",
    "- As the first step in any EDA\n",
    "- To detect outliers and skewness before modeling\n",
    "- To choose the right transformations (log for right-skewed data)\n",
    "- To compare groups (e.g. mean income by region)\n",
    "- To communicate data characteristics to stakeholders\n",
    "\n",
    "**Don't rely only on summary statistics:**\n",
    "- Always visualize data too (histograms, box plots, scatter plots)\n",
    "- Anscombe's quartet shows four datasets with identical mean, variance, correlation — but completely different shapes\n",
    "- Summary stats can hide multi-modality, non-linear relationships, and clustering"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a8b7c6d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Common Mistakes (Statistics-Specific Pitfalls)\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Reporting mean without checking for outliers/skew** — always check median too\n",
    "2. **Using population variance when you have a sample** — use `ddof=1`\n",
    "3. **Ignoring NaN values** — `np.mean` returns NaN if data has NaN; use `np.nanmean` or drop NaN first\n",
    "4. **Mode with no repeats** — `stats.mode` returns the first value; for continuous data the mode is ill-defined\n",
    "5. **Not looking at the distribution** — summary stats without a histogram can hide bimodality, skewness, or outliers\n",
    "6. **Comparing variance across different scales** — use coefficient of variation (std/mean) instead"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2a8b3c4d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Connection to Machine Learning\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Feature scaling** (standardization) uses mean and std: `z = (x - mean) / std`\n",
    "- **Outlier handling** (removal, winsorizing, transformation) is a key preprocessing step\n",
    "- **Log transformation** is common for right-skewed targets (house prices, income)\n",
    "- **EDA** with descriptive statistics helps choose the right model and loss function"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e3f5a7b8",
